  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="72">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 72</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-g-a">And þær se bonda sæt uncwydd ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wif ⁊ þa cild on þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ylcan unbesacan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-a">And þær se bonda sæt uncwyd ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif ⁊ þa cild on þam ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="72" corresp="#wit-q">Et ubi bónda (id est paterfamilias) mansit sine compellatione et calumpnia, sint uxor et pueri in eodem sine querela.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="72" corresp="#wit-b">And ðær se bunda sæt uncwyd [his deig] ⁊ unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif ⁊ ða cild [on þam ylcan] unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And þær se bonda sæt uncwydd his deig and unbecrafod, sitte þæt wif and þa cild on þam ylcan unbesacen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And when a householder has dwelt all his time free from claims and charges, his wife and children shall dwell [on the same property] unmolested by litigation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if a householder has remained free of claims and accusations during his lifetime, his wife and children may afterward hold that same property uncontested.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And where the householder dwelt undisturbed by charges and claims, the wife and children are to dwell on the same [property] unmolested by litigation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wo der freie Hausvater unangesprochen und unbeklagt (sein Lebtag B) gesessen hat, auf demselben [Hofe] sitze unbestritten die Ehefrau und die Kinder.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And where the free householder has sat unchallenged and unaccused (all his life, B), on that same [homestead] let the wife and the children sit undisputed.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="359"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Atr. 14</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 72-72:1: (III Atr 14)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="385"><label>shared formula</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>their formulaic 'æt uncwydd 7 unbecrafod'</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="472"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:IIIAtr_14">III Atr 14</ref> <quote>cf. III Ethelred, 14</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="385"><ref target="clause:Becwaeth_1">Becwæð</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Atr 14.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">cf. III Ethelred, 14</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">his deig: omitted GA, added in B in a sixteenth-century hand</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">on þam ylcan: omitted B</note>
      </div>
